//
// Description : FTInputBox: a message in the FT look with ONE field to type in, and the caller's own
//               button captions - the prompt that asks for a name. Shown in FTInputBox.dg.
//
// This code is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY;
// without even the implied warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.
//****************************************************************************
Use FTMessageBox.pkg        // FTMessageBoxText - the message's length picks the box's size

// FTInputBox.dg's dialog, once it exists; 0 until then.
Global_Variable Handle ghoFTInputBox
Move 0 to ghoFTInputBox

// FTInputBox.dg defines them - later than this package is compiled.
Register_Function FTShowInput String sTitle String sBodyHtml String sInputLabel String sValue ;
                              String sYesLabel String sNoLabel Returns Boolean
Register_Function FTInputValue Returns String

// The dialog - or 0: the program does not Use FTInputBox.dg, or its application object does not exist yet.
Function FTInputBoxPanel Global Returns Handle
    If (ghoApplication = 0) ;
        Function_Return 0
    Function_Return ghoFTInputBox
End_Function

/* A MESSAGE WITH ONE FIELD TO TYPE IN - FTHtmlMessage's box with a field under the message: a body written in
   HTML (paragraphs, bold, code samples - text in it already escaped), the field's label, and a verb on each
   button ("Rename now" / "Not now"). sValue goes in as the field's text and comes back as what was typed, when
   the first button (or Enter in the field) answers; on the second button or Esc it is left as it was. Returns
   True for the first button. sYesLabel "" is OK; sNoLabel "" gives one button.

   Windows has no box that asks for text, so where the dialog cannot show - a program that does not Use
   FTInputBox.dg, or before the application object exists - this answers False and leaves sValue alone.

       Move (sName + "X") to sNew
       Get FTInputBox ("Rename " + sName) sBodyHtml "Rename to:" (&sNew) "Rename now" "Not now" to bRename    */
Function FTInputBox Global String sTitle String sBodyHtml String sInputLabel String ByRef sValue ;
                           String sYesLabel String sNoLabel Returns Boolean
    Boolean bYes
    Handle hoPanel
    Move (FTInputBoxPanel()) to hoPanel
    If (hoPanel = 0) ;
        Function_Return False
    Get FTShowInput of hoPanel sTitle sBodyHtml sInputLabel sValue sYesLabel sNoLabel to bYes
    If (bYes) ;
        Get FTInputValue of hoPanel to sValue
    Function_Return bYes
End_Function
